Several indicators of decline in Taiwan's economy in the first quarter of the year - China News
Xinhua News Agency, Taipei, February 11 (reported by Zhao Bo and Huang Yang) - The export trade volume "连五黑" and the manufacturing purchasing managers index (PMI) have been contracting for seven consecutive months, and the consumer price index (CPI) has seen "3-digit" again... Recently, the Taiwan authority released the economic data of January 2023.
Experts believe that the Taiwan economy has not performed well at the beginning of the year and that growth pressure is not negligible.
According to the Ministry of Finance of Taiwan’s Treasury Affairs Bureau, Taiwan’s exports for January this year amounted to $31.51 billion, down 21.2% from last year and marking their fifth consecutive month of negative growth.
The export value of 11 major export commodities fell year-on-year in the same period.
Plastic rubber and its products and optical equipment suffered the greatest decline, with a year-on-year decline of 37.6 per cent and 35.7 per cent, respectively.
The export of electronic components fell by 20.1% year-on-year, the largest decline in 11 years.
Among them, the annual decline of integrated circuits was 18.3%, the biggest decline in 14 years.
Chai Mianna, the head of the Statistics Department, said that this showed that the weak demand for consumer electronics had spread, and the electronic industry was entering a correction period.
Statistics show that in January, Taiwan's imports and exports doubled, with the exports exceeding only $2.34 billion, the lowest level in almost three years.
The Taiwan authorities' financial services department believes that global terminal demand is declining, industry adjusts inventories to suppress the willingness of manufacturers to purchase, and exports are unlikely to improve in the short term, and Taiwan's exports decline in the first quarter of this year is more likely than expected.
According to the Taiwan Institute of Economic Research, in January this year, the Purchasing Managers’ Index (PMI) for manufacturing in Taiwan was revised down from 46.8% to 40.4%, with a decline of 3.3 percentage points compared to December last year and its seventh consecutive contraction.
In the economic monitoring index system, PMI is at 50% as the turning point for health and illness; an index greater than 50% indicates expansion of prosperity, while less than 50% signifies contraction.
In January, the five components of the PMI in Taiwan were tightened, including new orders, production and employment, and the delivery time of suppliers was shortened, and the inventory was tightened.
All six industries have returned a PMI contraction, and the order of contraction is as follows: the electricity and machinery industry (35.1%), the electronic and optical industry (35.2%), the chemical and biotechnology industry (39.2%), the basic raw materials industry (42.4%), the transportation industry (42.6%) and the food and textile industry (45.7%).
In terms of prices, the Taiwan authorities’ “Controller General Office” announced that the annual CPI growth rate in January this year was 3.04%, again breaking the 3% mark since July last year.
Among them, the price of vegetables rose by 28.25%, which was a 17-month high.
According to Cao Zhihong, a special commissioner of Taiwan’s “General Comptroller’s Office,” the increase in vegetable prices is indeed higher than expected, and if the Spring Festival factor is excluded, the average CPI in January and February should be close to the 2.71% of last December, and inflationary pressures are still present and remain high.
In a comprehensive report on the Taiwan economy this year, based on local media reports from the United Press, Yahoo Finance and others, experts expressed pessimism.
Wu Da-ren, a professor of the Department of Economics at the Central University of Taiwan, analyzed that the export slump may cause the cash flow of export manufacturers to be problematic, and the default risk will increase.
At the same time, the reduction in orders has led manufacturers to reduce labour costs, affecting the labour market and household economies, which in turn impacts on consumer power.
Chiou Tsa-sheng, a researcher at the Institute of Taiwanese Economic Research, believes that the inflationary situation in Europe and the United States has not been resolved, and the demand continues to shrink. He predicts that the export decline in Taiwan will continue until the first half of the year.
As the Taiwan economy is export-driven and is affected by export slowdown, the overall growth performance will be lower than last year.
Did the Balloon Incident Brighten America's Eyes?
Strengthening restrictions on technology exports to China
According to the Wall Street Journal today, the US is preparing to tighten its technology exports to China further after the balloon incident.
Current and former security officials have said that the balloon incident highlights the national security threat posed by China, and will seek more political support for strengthening US technology protection.
The US claims that the balloon carried antennas and sensors for intelligence gathering and communications.
According to Martijn Rasser, a senior official of the former US Central Intelligence Agency and now serving at the New American Security Center in Washington, D.C.
This is undoubtedly fueling the fire of hardliners in support of US-China tough talk.
White House press secretary Karine Jean-Pierre said Thursday that "we will consider taking more sweeping action to expose and counter China's broader surveillance activities, which pose a threat to our national security and our allies and partners."
US officials said they had informed more than 30 governments about the balloon incident, and that international coordination was crucial to address the Chinese threat.
Emily Benso, a senior researcher at the Center for Strategic and International Studies, says that, in addition to the Biden administration’s actions, the newly formed House Committee on Strategic Competition between the US and the Chinese Communist Party may also put pressure on the US to take tougher measures to slow China’s development.
She says that members of Congress will feel increasing pressure to take more assertive positions, which may in turn force the White House to adopt even stronger policies.
The Wall Street Journal reported that many advocates of stricter export controls are also pushing to expand the scope of the controls to include artificial intelligence and other industries.
The US government is also in the process of developing an investment review plan to assess whether there are potential national security threats from China to its overseas investments.
Analysts say the White House may face pressure to move faster on the plan.
The first individual pension products have been launched, with minimum holding period of 360 days - Xinhua News Agency
The first individual pension products have been launched.
The 7 products offered by the home institution can be selected, with the shortest holding period being 360 days.
Personal pension investment products are finally available.
On February 10, China Finance Network released the first batch of personal pension fund management products. The personal pension fund management products of Agricultural Bank of China, Industrial and Commercial Bank of China and China Post Group officially went on sale.
At last, the “shelf” of personal pension accounts is complete with four products – personal pension savings, personal pension investment, personal pension insurance, and personal pension open-end funds.
It was described that the first set of personal pension products, all of which are public equity net-value open-ended products, of which five are new products, two are existing products, and except for one product is a mixed product, the remaining six products are all fixed-income products.
The reporter of Beijing Youth Daily saw that 4 of the 5 new products were from ICBC Wealth Management, all of which were fixed-income products with the shortest holding period of 365 days, 540 days, 720 days and 1080 days, and the corresponding performance benchmarks (annualized) were 3.70% - 4.20%, 4.10% - 4.60%, 4.40% - 4.90% and 5.25% - 5.75%, respectively.
The remaining new product is "Post and Telecom Wealth Add Joy - Harmony Shortest Holding for 1095 Days No. 1", which is also a fixed-income product. It started fundraising on February 10th and ended on February 19th. The risk level is Level II.
Among the two maturing products, one is the Agricultural Bank of China (ABC) “In Harmony and Dynamic” 360-day technology innovation RMB wealth management product, which is a mixed-type investment product with a risk level of three.
The second ongoing product is “Post and Express Wealth Add Joy - Harmony Shortest Holding for 365 Days No. 1,” which is of fixed income type. It started fundraising on December 30 last year and officially began operations on January 4 this year. Its cumulative net asset value as of February 8 was 1.0011.
According to the State Council Office's Opinion on Promoting the Development of Personal Pensions, the funds of the personal pension fund account can be invested in financial products such as bank accounts, savings deposits, commercial pension insurance, public equity funds, etc.
The launch of the first individual pension product marks that investors in the individual pension can officially purchase products through their individual pension funds accounts.
In November last year, the China Insurance Regulatory and Supervisory Commission formulated the “Interim Measures for the Management of Individual Pension Business of Commercial Banks and Wealth Management Companies”.
The Scheme provides that participants may purchase personal pension products such as personal retirement savings, personal retirement financial products, personal retirement insurance products, and personal retirement public fund products through the personal retirement fund account.
Subsequently, the Ministry of Human Resources and Social Security, the Ministry of Finance, and the State Administration of Taxation issued a notice to clarify that the individual pension plan will be implemented in 36 pilot cities and regions, including Beijing, Tianjin, and Hebei Shijiazhuang and the Xiongan New Area, Shanxi Jincheng City, and other cities and regions.
By the end of 2022, the number of individual pension participants will be 19.54 million, and the number of contributors will be 6.13 million, with a total contribution amount of 14.2 billion yuan.
Previously, participating banks had only introduced three products for pilot testing: individual pension savings, individual pension insurance, and individual public offering funds.
With the launch of personal pension investment products, how should investors choose?
The experts of the Research and Development Department of the Bank of Investments said that, compared with other personal pension products, the pension product in the pilot phase and the personal pension product have three characteristics.
First, the banks are more robust, with more robust risk management mechanisms, investment strategies and concepts, and independent third-party custodianship by non-mother banks.
Second, the long-term nature of the product. The term of the pension products in the pilot phase is five years or more, and the next-stage issue of the personal pension product will have a minimum holding period of one year in principle, with an encouragement to hold for more than three years.
Third, the product is universal, with a low threshold for purchase, usually starting at 1 yuan, and some as low as 0.01 yuan, and the rates of the products &apos; custody fees, management fees, etc. are more favourable.
Professionals point out that investors should choose products based on their characteristics and risk tolerance.
The personal pension savings have the characteristics of long period, high interest rate and high security, which are suitable for the people with low risk tolerance; the personal pension insurance products are more emphasis on protection, which are suitable for the people who cannot bear the investment risk and can accept the stable income; the personal pension investment products and public fund products are not guaranteed and not guaranteed the income, but the expected income is relatively high, which are suitable for the people with certain financial knowledge and high risk tolerance.
Written by reporters of Beijing News, Cheng Yi, and coordinated by Qiu Hai Bo.
Newly Appointed Members of the Central Committee, Alternate Members, and Provincial and Ministerial Level Main Leaders Complete Study Course on Learning and Implementing Xi Jinping Thought on Socialism with Chinese Characteristics for a New Era and the 20th National Congress Spirit - Rolling News - Huasheng Online - Hunan Daily
The Central Committee of the CPC, the Standing Committee of the Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee, and the leading cadres of the provincial and ministerial level studied and implemented the essence of Xi Jinping Thought on Socialism with Chinese Characteristics for a New Era and the spirit of the 20th CPC National Congress.
2023-02-11 13:07:20 [Source: Xinhua News Agency] [Editor: Li Xufeng] [Font:【大 中 小】
Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, February 10 (covering the afternoon) - The study of the 20th CPC National Congress and the 20th CPC National Congress on the implementation of the new era of socialism with Chinese characteristics and the new members of the Central Committee, the Standing Committee of the Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee, the leading cadres of the provincial-level departments and the leading cadres of the ministries and commissions attended the closing ceremony of the study of the implementation of the new era of socialism with Chinese characteristics and the 20th CPC National Congress in the Central Party School (the National Academy of Public Administration) on the 10th. Xi Jinping, a member of the Standing Committee of the Political Bureau of the CPC Central Committee and the Secretary of the Central Secretariat of the CPC Central Committee, made a summary speech.
He said that the Chinese people should learn in depth from the spirit of the important speech of General Secretary Xi Jinping at the opening ceremony of the seminar, more firmly uphold the principle of "two establishments" and firmly do the "two defences", strengthen their skills, take serious action, and firmly advance the work of Chinese-style modernization, and achieve results that can be tested by history, practice and the people in the comprehensive construction of a socialist modernized state and the comprehensive promotion of the great revival of the Chinese nation.
During the seminar, all participants were guided by Xi Jinping's ideas of socialism with Chinese characteristics in the new era, carefully studied the spirit of the 20th Party Congress and the important speech of the General Secretary Xi Jinping at the opening ceremony of the seminar, and engaged in in-depth discussions and exchanges in connection with practical activities. They deepened their understanding of a series of major theoretical and practical issues of Chinese-style modernization, strengthened their confidence and determination to comprehensively advance the great revival of the Chinese nation with Chinese-style modernization under the strong leadership of the Party Central Committee, with Comrade Xi Jinping as its core, and strengthened their sense of responsibility and mission to fulfil their duties, do their work well and ensure a good start to the new era.
At the graduation ceremony, 10 representatives made speeches and shared their learning experience.
Chai Qi stated that learning and implementing the thought of socialism with Chinese characteristics for a new era under Xi Jinping’s leadership is both an urgent political task for the present and in the future as well, and should be carried out according to the requirements of “comprehensive study, comprehensive grasp, and comprehensive implementation.” It is necessary to push forward the work on learning and implementing it further down deep, more solidly, and deeper into people's hearts.
To more deeply understand the decisive significance of “the two establishments,” we must resolutely uphold the core position of Xi Jinping and the authority of the Central Committee with Comrade Xi at its heart, as well as the centralized and unified leadership of the Party. We should continuously enhance our political judgment, political insight, and political execution, ensuring that we always maintain high consistency in thought, politics, and action with the Central Committee led by Comrade Xi.
We must strive to master the basic knowledge of Marxist theory, consciously armed our minds with the Party's innovative theory, guide our practice and promote our work, and make every effort to study in depth, understand thoroughly and work with determination, truly learning to be firm in our convictions, learn absolute loyalty and learn to fulfil our mission.
We must implement the decisions of the 20th National Congress of the Party with a spirit of enthusiasm and commitment, firmly advance the Chinese-style modernization, roll up our sleeves and get ready, and act as a good "construction team leader" to turn the blueprint into reality step by step.
We must keep in mind that the comprehensive and strict control of the Party is always on the way, and the Party's self-revolution is always on the way. We must firmly implement the political responsibility of the comprehensive and strict control of the Party, and take the political construction of the Party as our guiding principle, and make a great stride forward in the new great project of building the Party of the new era.
We should strengthen our ability to promote high-quality development, serve the people, and prevent and resolve risks, and promote the investigation and research spirit, resolutely prevent and overcome formalism and bureaucracy.
Shi Taifeng, Li Ganjie, Li Shulei, Chen Wenqing, Liu Jinguo, Wang Xiaohong attended the graduation ceremony, and Chen Hi presided over the graduation ceremony.
East Germany's last Communist Prime Minister is dead.
The successor of the East German Communist Party reported in a party statement, “Last night, Hans Modrow left us at the age of 95.
Therefore, our party lost an important leader.
Translation requested.
On November 13, 1989, four days after the Berlin Wall was opened to reunite East and West Berlin, Modrow had said he would help turn East Germany into a democratic state.
At the time, the Communist Party leaders were forced to resign because of protests demanding democracy and freedom in the East.
When Mikhail Gorbachev came to power in the Soviet Union, he called for change in Soviet-dominated Eastern Europe.
On March 1990, Modrow announced the first and only free election of the German Democratic Republic (GDR).
The election result led to his resignation as Prime Minister.
Despite the reforms, opponents accused him of trying to delay the political change and unification that took place in October 1990.
He was also criticized for trying to rebuild, rather than abolish, the secret police.
In 1993, Modrow was convicted of electoral fraud in the May 1989 municipal elections, but he was not jailed.
These allegations were allegedly politically motivated.
From 1990 to 1994, Modrow continued to serve in the German Bundestag and from 1999 to 2004, he was a Member of the European Parliament.
Mr. Modro sees himself as a reformer and wants to change the Communist Party from within.
In 1999, he told Reuters he did not want East Germany to return, but said East Germany's achievements should be acknowledged.
Mordor was born in 1928 in the German town of Jasenitz (now Jasienica in Poland) and received training as a machinist.
During World War II, he served as an officer of the Young Firemen’s Battalion and became a member of the Volkssturm, a militia organization that conscripted men aged 16 to 60 for the final struggle of the war.
At the age of 17, Modrow was captured by the Soviet army and taken as a prisoner of war to the Soviet Union, where he attended anti-Fascist courses and became a committed Communist.
In 1949, the year East Germany was founded, he returned to the country and found a job as a mechanical engineer and continued his studies in social sciences and economics, earning a doctorate.
Modrow was a staff member of the Free German Youth Movement, which almost all East German youth joined, and was promoted to the position of president of the Dresden Regional Party from 1973 to 1989 through the ruling Social Democratic Union Party (SED).
He has also been a member of the East German parliament for more than 30 years.
In 1990, Modrow became the de facto leader of East Germany and held the highest state office.
VNA Hanoi - VNA correspondents reported that the official visit to Singapore and Brunei by Vietnamese Prime Minister Pham Minh Chinh and his wife has been a complete success, yielding comprehensive, practical and specific results.
In the three days of his visit to Singapore and Brunei, Premier Feng Mingping attended more than 30 different events.
The achievements have injected new impetus into the development of the strategic partnership and comprehensive partnership between Vietnam and New Zealand in a more profound, more comprehensive and effective direction.
During his visit to the two countries, Prime Minister Pham Minh Chinh continued to reiterate the foreign policy of the Vietnamese Party and State, namely independence, diversity, flexibility, willingness to be a good friend and a reliable partner of all countries, and a responsible member of the international community.
Strengthening relations with Singapore and Brunei is in the interests of both countries, and is aimed at improving the well-being of their people, and at peace, stability and development in the region and the world.
At the meetings and talks, Pham Minh Chinh, Prime Minister, agreed with the leaders of Singapore and Brunei to continue to strengthen political trust with Vietnam through the high-level delegation visits, effective implementation of the various bilateral cooperation mechanisms and important cooperation agreements.
Many cooperation documents were signed during the visit.
Among these, two major highlights include the Memorandum of Understanding on Green and Digital Economy Partnership signed with Singapore and the Action Plan for Strengthening Comprehensive Partnership between Vietnam and Brunei Darussalam for the 2023-2027 Period.
Vietnam and Singapore signed a Memorandum of Understanding on Green and Digital Economy Partnership.
Photo credit: VNA
Vingroup President Nguyen Phu Trong stressed during meetings with business leaders, seminars or at economic forums that Vietnam is open to and ready to create favorable conditions for Singaporean and Bruneian companies to expand their investments in digital transformation, green energy, high-tech, innovation and creativity sectors in the country.
The visit not only helped to deepen Viet Nam &apos; s cooperation with Singapore and Brunei in various traditional areas of politics, diplomacy, economy, security, defence, education and training, oil and gas, tourism, civil exchanges, etc., but also created a framework for cooperation between the countries in new potential areas such as digital economy, green economy, energy transition, innovative ideas, smart cities, sustainable development, etc.
King of Brunei Hassanal Bolkiah and Prime Minister of Viet Nam Pham Minh Chinh are preparing to enter the bilateral meeting.
Photo credit: VNA
During his visits to the two countries, Prime Minister Pham Minh Chinh arranged time to visit and listen to the thoughts and aspirations of the Vietnamese diaspora living in the two countries.
At the meeting with the leaders of the two countries, Pham Minh Chinh, Prime Minister of Vietnam, suggested that the authorities of both countries pay more attention to the fair treatment of the Vietnamese people in the host country, create conditions for the local Vietnamese community to contribute to the local society, and create favorable conditions for the development of bilateral relations.
The proposal has been agreed to and supported by both leaders of the two countries.
In particular, Prime Minister Pham Minh Chinh also shared with leaders of the two countries the desire for a united, peaceful, stable and prosperous ASEAN community; and agreed to maintain unity and cooperation with ASEAN countries and enhance the central role of ASEAN in the regional and international context of complex and volatile.
With the important results achieved, Prime Minister Phan Minh Triet &apos; s official visits to Singapore and Brunei contributed positively to the effective implementation of the outward route of the Thirteenth Congress of the Communist Party of Vietnam, which prioritizes the strengthening of relations with ASEAN neighbours, the effective implementation of the Conclusion No. 12 of the Political Bureau of the Communist Party of Vietnam on the work of Vietnamese expatriates in the new situation (12-KL/TW) and the use of the strength of all-national solidarity.
(continued)
NEWS GOV-MO: Police announcement: Police Department calls on citizens to beware of fake telecom companies scam text messages
Recently, the Department of Police received several telecom fraud cases, criminals fake Australian Telecommunications Company to the owner of the fraudulent text message attached to the website link, with the credits expiring as soon as possible to redeem the prize as a bait, lure the owner to log into a fake website to redeem.
The owner entered the credit card details and the verification code as instructed and immediately received a notification from the financial institution that the credit card had an unknown consumption record and that the credit card details were suspected of having been stolen from the aforementioned website.
Upon investigation, it was confirmed that the relevant telecommunications companies did not send out the aforementioned messages.
The Police Department urges citizens to be vigilant if they receive such mobile text messages and not to click on the website links contained in the text messages or provide any personal information; if they are asked to provide credit card information, account transaction passwords, transaction verification codes, they should be extra careful to prevent credit card theft.
Anti-fraud reminder:
1. Pay more attention to cybersecurity information and raise personal awareness of prevention;
2. Do not log in to websites with unknown origins and register your personal information and credit card information on the website, so as to avoid being stolen by others.
3. Be vigilant against fake and phishing websites and always check that the URLs of the websites are fully consistent with the official ones;
4. Install antivirus software for mobile phones, mobile devices or computers and update it regularly;
5. If you suspect you have been scammed or committed a crime, you should immediately call the Police Fraud Check Hotline at 8800 7777 or report to the Police Hotline at 993 for assistance.
EU summit debates refugee policy, EU officials: reception process is a bottleneck - China News Network
EU summit struggles over migrant policy, EU official: Every step of the process is a bottleneck
【Global Times reporter in Belgium, Ni Ruifeng】According to the report of the French news agency on February 10, at the latest EU summit held that day, the President of the European Commission, von der Leyen, said that the leaders of the EU agreed to issue stricter policies on illegal immigration to make it easier to expel illegal immigrants.
The EU's move is a response to the growing problem of illegal immigration in Europe, and now the core issue is that the number of illegal immigrants who can be deported is very small.
According to the document, the EU leaders called on the Commission "to immediately mobilize a large amount of EU funds" to strengthen the external borders with infrastructure and surveillance.
Yet, there is bitter disagreement between the EU and its member states over payment of fence-related costs.
Von der Leyen has repeatedly stated that EU funds will not cover the costs involved.
But some diplomats from member countries said that if the EU could shoulder some of the cost of installing cameras, observation towers and other infrastructure along the external borders, it would free up national budgets to speed up construction.
According to the European Euractiv website, EU officials have admitted that bottlenecks exist at every step of the refugee reception process, that limited reception capacity and overburdened immigration authorities in member states cannot prevent refugees from filing “numerous” asylum applications across the EU, and that the EU’s reception system is in an almost “eternal crisis.”
According to the European Commission, the number of asylum applications received by Schengen countries last year was more than 92,000, an increase of nearly half compared to the previous year.
Meanwhile, the EU recorded more than 330,000 illegal entry cases last year.
In this context, the summit also agreed on a "principle" that EU member states can deport illegal immigrants to their home countries based on a court ruling of another member state.
Moreover, it is reported that EU leaders also agreed to “increase the use of the concept of ‘safe states’,” which will pave the way for the EU to develop a common list.
(Source: Global Times; Author: Liu Ruifei)
Sumwalt, the Vice President of the KMT, delivered the message of Sung Tsun-ying: welcome the green camp to visit the mainland under the 92 consensus
Taiwan China Nationalist Party Vice Chairman Xia Liuyan met with both the State Councilor and Premier of the People's Republic of China, Wang Linqing, and the Director-General of the Office of the Central People’s Government in the Taiwan Area, Song Tao, on separate occasions this time.
Zhao Chunshan, senior advisor to the Nationalist Party’s official State Policy Foundation, was interviewed by the Taiwan Central News Agency last night, and gave a positive evaluation of Song’s statement that as long as the Green Camp members agree with the “Consensus of 1992” and are against Taiwan’s independence, China welcomes them to visit the mainland.
The National Party has considered it a fresh development.
Xia Liyan met with Song Tao earlier that day, but the news did not mention this claim.
The ruling Democratic Progressive Party of Taiwan has repeatedly clarified its refusal to accept the “Consensus of 2005.”
According to Central News Agency, the Central Committee of the Kuomintang (KMT) led by Vice Chairman Shieh Liang-ying visited China and met with the Politburo member of the Central Committee of the Communist Party of China (CPC) Wang Hongbing, the new head of the Taiwanese Affairs Office of the CPC Central Committee, and the Party Secretary of Beijing City Committee, Yan Q everybody.
Xia Liying and Song Tao met to discuss the political foundation of the CPC and the anti-Taiwan independence, and Zhao Chunshan, a senior advisor of the Nationalist Party, said that the "92 Consensus" of the Nationalist Party was the original "92 Consensus".
Zhao Chunshan analyzed that this felt different from the previous meetings he had attended.
Recently, I had a video conference with scholars from the mainland, and this time, I did not hear any scholars talking about the unification and the “anti-secession law”. Instead, I heard the restoration of exchanges and dialogues.
Zhao Chunshan pointed out that the cross-strait situation is tense and dangerous, and the mainland hopes to convey the intention of improving relations through the Kuomintang.
Because there is no mutual trust between the CPC and the other party, the latter is still willing to work well for the Taiwanese, and the delegate does not want to damage relations between the two sides.
According to Zhao Chunshan, Wang Shuning also personally instructed Song Tao to say, “They (Taiwan farmers and fishermen) have made demands, you must implement them,” and if they cannot be resolved in a comprehensive way, they will be dealt with on a case-by-case basis.
The report did not mention whether the Nationalist Party delegation visiting the mainland directly referred to the daily overflights of Chinese military aircraft and warships, the agricultural and fisheries problems in Taiwan's few counties and cities, or whether the Central News Agency reporters were interviewed to raise such issues.
What was the mysterious object that crashed in Alaska's airspace?
Confusing and contradictory, speculation rife.
On Friday afternoon (10 February), the United States military again used the most advanced American stealth jet fighter F-22 to shoot down an unidentified object flying over Alaska, United States.
The landing site was ten miles off the coast of Alaska.
This was the second time in less than a week that the US forces shot down an aerial flying object.
Last Saturday, a spy balloon from China was shot down off the coast of South Carolina, several days after drifting over US airspace.
The Pentagon said that the second object downed Thursday night first entered US airspace over Alaska’s northeast and was tracked by US military as it moved at an altitude of 12,000 meters (39,000 feet) in size about the same as a small car, much smaller than the earlier Chinese spy balloon downed.
The Pentagon also believes that there is no current indication that the object is manipulable.
John Corby, the White House National Security Council's Strategic Communications Coordinator, said on Friday that while the exact appearance of the high-altitude object was not clear, it "posed a reasonable threat to the safety of civil aviation."
Kobe said that the object was different from the spy balloon found in the United States, as it did not have the words "payload" written on it.
Kobe said, "We call it a 'thing' because that's the best description we can make of it right now."
President Biden listened to the Pentagon’s advice before ordering the object to be shot down, and he was “very careful” in making that decision, Corby added.
The United States official description of the object can be summarized roughly as: the size of a small car, without joysticks, without suspension, flying at an altitude of about 10,000 metres.
But these data do not answer basic questions such as what this object is, which country it belongs to, and what mission it is performing.
Many analyses and speculations on the Internet now suggest that this may be another Chinese balloon.
It may have come from China, as did the spy balloon that invaded US airspace and the Chinese balloon that hovered over Latin America, both of which were performing a mission in different locations.
Some have also linked the Alaskan "object" to "unidentified flying objects" (UFOs).
The report in the US News & World Report cites former US Congressman Peter Meijer’s tweet on Friday that he hopes this “unidentified flying object” is an espionage balloon rather than a legitimate UFO.
“The irony of mixing alien spacecraft with weather balloons is surprising, but it is not worth triggering an interstellar conflict,” says Mayer.
Meeks tweeted this shortly after Kobe confirmed that the object in Alaska had been shot down.
The Newsweek said that it was not only Mejer who suspected the object was a UFO.
Republican Rep. Tim Burchett from Tennessee criticized the government’s cover-up last month, calling on the Office of the Director of National Intelligence (DNI) to publish a report on “unidentified flying objects.”
Xi Jinping's Letter to the Members of the Chinese Medical Team in Africa Encourages Them to Practice Compassionate Medicine to Benefit the Local People and to Tell the Story of China with Real Actions - News - Hunan Daily - Huanxi Shibao
Xi Jinping's letter to encourage China's medical teams in Africa to serve local people with compassion and skill, and tell China's story through concrete actions
2023-02-11 13:09:10 [Source: Xinhua News Agency] [Editor: Li Xufeng] [Font:【大 中 小】
Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, February 10 - General Secretary of the CPC Central Committee, President of the People's Republic of China and Chairman of the Central Military Commission Xi Jinping sent a letter to the 19th batch of medical team to the Central African Republic on February 9, expressing his greetings to them and all the medical teams abroad and making a sincere wish.
In his reply, Xi Jinping said that you have overcome difficulties in work and life in the Central African Republic, and have served the local people with your heart, and you are both a white angel of rescue and a friendly ambassador.
This year marks the 60th anniversary of the dispatch of the Chinese medical team to aid foreign countries. I would like to extend my sincere condolences to the comrades who are currently and have been carrying out medical aid missions abroad.
Xi Jinping pointed out that the Chinese people love peace and cherish life, and medical aid is a vivid embodiment of this.
I hope that you will not forget your original purpose and mission, and will strive to promote the spirit of the Chinese medical team, which is fearless, willing to sacrifice, to save lives, to help injured people and to show unlimited love, and that you will benefit the local people with your kindness and skill, tell the story of China through practical action, and make a greater contribution to promoting the building of a community of human health and health.
Foreign medical assistance is an important component of China's foreign aid work.
In 1963, China sent its first medical team abroad to Algeria.
Over the past 60 years, China has dispatched 30,000 medical teams to 76 countries and regions in Africa, Asia, the Americas, Europe and Oceania, treating 290 million patients, and winning the international community &apos; s recognition.
Currently, the medical team is working in 115 medical points in 56 countries around the world, of which nearly half are in remote and difficult areas.
Recently, 11 members of the 19th batch of China’s medical teams dispatched to Central Africa wrote letters to President Xi Jinping, reporting on their efforts in implementing the spirit of the 20th CPC National Congress and providing medical services for local residents, as well as expressing their determination to contribute to building a community with a shared future for mankind.
Iran celebrates anniversary of revolution Hackers who support protests shock president's TV speech
The Islamic Republic of Iran held an official rally on Saturday to mark the 44th anniversary of the Iranian revolution, but anti-government hackers briefly interrupted President Ibrahim Raisi’s television address.
The president's televised address was interrupted for about a minute on the internet, and a screen appeared with the symbol of the Iranian hackers group "Edalat Ali" (Ali's Justice).
There was also a voice shouting "Death to the Islamic Republic."
According to Reuters reports today, Iran is commemorating the anniversary of the revolution, and hackers have interrupted the national television coverage.
As Iran officially commemorates the 44th anniversary of the Iranian revolution, Raisi’s hardline government faces the boldest challenge from young protesters who are calling for its ouster, but Raisi still calls on “deceived youth” to repent so that they can be pardoned by Iran’s supreme leader.
Nationwide protests have continued in Iran since the death of 22-year-old Mahsa Amini while in the custody of the country's morality police.
The Iranian security forces’ deadly crackdown on protests is one of the strongest challenges the Islamic Republic has faced since the 1979 revolution overthrew the 2,500-year-old monarchy.
As part of an amnesty in celebration of the anniversary of the revolution, Iranian authorities freed Friday two political prisoners who had been on hunger strike: Farkhaddin Mesbah-Yazdi and Fariba Adel-Haeri, an Iranian-French scholar.
Earlier, Supreme Leader Ayatollah Ali Khamenei issued an amnesty that included some of the prisoners arrested during recent anti-government protests.
According to the Human Rights Activists News Agency (HRANA), as of Friday, 528 protesters had been killed, including 71 minors.
The report says that 70 government security personnel were killed.
It is believed that up to 19,763 protesters were arrested.
For weeks, Iranian leaders and the official media have been calling for voting at Saturday &apos; s rallies to show opposition to the protests and support for the Government.
On Friday night, the night of the Iranian Revolution’s anniversary, the official media showed fireworks as part of the government-sponsored celebrations, with people shouting “Allahu Akbar!”
“(God is the greatest!)”
However, there is also much shouting in assemblies of “Dictator must die!”
"Death of the Islamic Republic" in a video posted on social media.
On Saturday, Government television broadcast live video of the official gatherings in the states throughout the country.
In Tehran, as part of the official celebrations, domestically produced anti-ballistic missiles, drones, anti-submarine cruisers and other military equipment were displayed.
President Lesley’s speeches were frequently interrupted by the slogan “America Die” – a symbol of the state’s rallying.
The crowd also chanted "Death to Israel."
Adelkhah, who has been in prison since 2019, is one of seven French nationals detained in Iran, Reuters said, a factor in the deterioration of relations between Paris and Tehran in recent months.
She was sentenced to five years in prison in 2020 for national security offences.
They then put her under house arrest at home, but in January she was returned to prison.
Adelkhah denied these allegations.
A week before his release, Mesami’s supporters warned that he was at risk of death as a result of his hunger strike protests.
He was arrested in 2018 for protesting the mandatory wearing of the headscarf.
The French Foreign Ministry called for Adelkhah’s release on Friday, calling for her freedom to be restored, “including her being allowed to return to France if she so wishes.”
