The 16th China-Japan Energy Saving and Environmental Protection Comprehensive Forum was held in Beijing. He Lifeng attended the main forum and delivered a keynote speech - China News
Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, February 11 - The 16th China-Japan Energy Saving and Environmental Protection Comprehensive Forum was held in Beijing on the 11th of February with a combination of online and offline ways.
Hu Lifeng, member of the Standing Committee of the CPC Central Committee and Director of the National Development and Reform Commission, delivered a keynote speech at the main forum.
Huang Lifeng noted that hosting this forum is an important step in implementing the consensus reached at the joint meeting between President Xi Jinping and Prime Minister Fumio Kishida in Bangkok to strengthen green development cooperation between China and Japan.
China will fully implement the spirit of the 20th CPC National Congress, accelerate the green transformation of development, deepen the prevention and control of environmental pollution, comprehensively strengthen resource conservation, actively and steadily promote carbon peaking and carbon neutrality, promote the coordinated reduction of carbon, pollution, greening, and growth, and promote ecological priority, resource conservation, and low-carbon, green development.
China is willing to work with Japan to deepen green and low-carbon industry cooperation, technology cooperation, policy dialogue and cultural exchange, and promote the development of green cooperation between the two countries to a new level.
Japanese Minister of Economy, Trade and Industry Shunji Watanabe attended the main forum and delivered a keynote speech.
The forum is jointly organized by the National Development and Reform Commission of China, the Ministry of Commerce of China, the Ministry of Economy and Trade of Japan, and the Japanese-Chinese Economic Association, featuring a main forum and four sub-forums on energy efficiency improvement, automotive electrification and automation, hydrogen energy, and long-term trade between China and Japan.
Representatives from the governments, enterprises and institutions of both China and Japan attended the exchange.
Hunan Questions and Answers: How to View the Employment Data in the United States in January and the Future Trend - Economic Observer - A Professional Financial News Website
Q: How do you view the January non-farm employment data in the United States, which exceeded expectations, and the future trends?
A: On February 3, the US Department of Labor released the employment data of non-agricultural employment in January 2023. The number of new non-agricultural employment was 517,000, which was much higher than the market expectations of 189,000; the unemployment rate fell to 3.4%, which was the lowest level in the past 50 years; the average hourly wage growth was 4.4%, which was slightly slower than the previous month.
From a total perspective, this data is subject to many one-off and technical factors of disturbance, such as teachers returning from strike, adjustments in survey statistics, updates on seasonal adjustment factors, etc., which may be revised (refer to the downward revision of non-farm payroll employment for January 2022 from 5.04 million to 3.64 million). Non-farm payroll employment may not be as strong as it appears in the data.
From the perspective of structure, the layoff impact of high-tech enterprises is still there, but the proportion is relatively low; the employment of high-contact service industries such as leisure hotels, education and health care has increased significantly, and the labor shortage of the service industry is still there.
Combined with a similarly over-expected recovery in the services PMI, job vacancy and labor gap data, and strong consumer credit data, we judge that the US services sector is recovering rapidly after extreme weather and holidays.
We believe that the tightness of the U.S. labor market will not improve without a recession.
At present, the supply gap of the US labor market is still more than 5 million, and the labor participation rate is rising slowly, especially the labor participation rate of 25-54-year-olds has reached the peak before the epidemic.
Moreover, because of strong excess saving and consumption credit among US residents, the strength of consumer demand will further delay the impact on employment markets from tightening policies.
The tight labor market in the US will be the bottom color of the US economy in 2023.
The combination of the near-ending of the tightening cycle and the repeated fluctuation of inflation expectations is not optimistic about the continuous decline of wage growth.
Prior to the release of the data, the US stock, bond and foreign exchange markets were overly optimistic about the path of interest rate hikes by the Federal Reserve.
As inflation data continues to improve, the Fed is slowing its rate hikes while maintaining a fragile balance of market inflation expectations. But markets are ignoring the Fed’s hawk-like statements, expecting not only an early halt to the hikes, but two rate cuts at the end of the year.
In the context of tight labor market and the impact of tightening policies, we believe that the guidance of the Federal Reserve on the end of the year is relatively reasonable. The adjustment of extreme expectations and the congestion of trading will cause some damage to the market.
However, the persistence of wage growth will not reverse the current rapidly declining trend in inflation. As M2 data turns negative year-on-year and the leading indicators of the various CPI sub-elements gradually improve, the US CPI data has moved into a rapidly declining phase since October, the persistence of wage growth will only form a base for future inflation data, and the current market expectations are difficult to falsify, and the market will enter a new round of play after the next inflation data is released.
Shenzhen: Building the first and leading city of extreme speed pioneers in China - China News Service
China News Service, February 11 - According to the "Shenzhen Industry and Information" WeChat public number, the Shenzhen Municipal Industry and Information Bureau recently issued the "Shenzhen Action Plan for the Construction of the Ultra-Fast City".
It is proposed that by the end of 2023, a super broadband network with high rates, large capacity, and low latency will be built to achieve the goal of “Dual Gigabit, Full Optical Network, 1 millisecond, Everything Connected,” making it China’s first and world-leading city in terms of ultra-fast speed.
The Plan proposes to accelerate the upgrade of the gigabit optical network.
By the end of 2023, the share of 10G PON ports will reach 100%, and the number of all-optical industrial parks (industrial parks) will exceed 100.
The Plan calls for a comprehensive improvement in the energy efficiency of 5G networks.
Research on the development of Shenzhen 5G network service quality standards, conducting 5G network testing assessments, and improving the quality of 5G network services.
Support the operators of basic telecommunications to increase the optimization of 5G networks in key areas and places, and add 10,000 5G base stations throughout the year. The average download speed in the city will reach 500 Mbps, and the upload speed will reach 100 Mbps. The download speed in key areas will reach 1 Gbps, and the upload speed will reach 200 Mbps. The network speed and user experience will be greatly improved.
Build a high-quality wireless local area network at the city level.
To establish a standard for public WLAN services, to promote the upgrade of WLAN in areas with dense population and information consumption needs in all districts of the city, and to provide 1000Mbps access capability.
Based on “Deep iNet”, a unified authentication and supervision platform for public wireless local area networks across the city is being constructed to achieve one-time authentication with seamless roaming and intelligent switching, supporting operators to integrate social self-built APs (wireless access points) with the authentication supervision platform.
By the end of 2023, the total number of upgraded access points will be no less than 20,000.
In addition, the plan also proposed to build a high-quality full-wavelength network, build a multi-tiered calculation supply system, accelerate the construction of key communication network facilities, and improve the ability of Internet application service.
The plan clearly states that collaborative construction of an IoT perception system will be carried out.
The city will explore the possibility of building a management model for the construction of urban sensing terminals based on the "open source Hongmon" operating system, reducing the cost of connection, accelerating the construction of a city-level IoT sensing platform, and promoting the urban IoT platform, the network of professional IoT platforms in various fields, and the data interconnection.
Deepen the application of IoT sensing in the fields of urban management, public services, public safety, transportation and travel, and expand the collection of fixed sensing data in urban roads, buildings, public facilities and mobile sensing data in smart connected cars.
By the end of 2023, the number of water, electricity, gas, and intelligent sensing terminals will exceed 9 million, and 20 multi-functional smart poles will be built.
The plan also mentions the strengthening of satellite and ground communications integration applications, the development of low-air network infrastructure, and the advancement of deep coverage of 5G networks at sea.
At the same time, it will promote deep coverage of the 5G network at sea, build an ecosystem for industrial innovation and development, and support the organization of top-level events and events.
(China New Finance)
China’s e-commerce industry is emerging with a “new variable”, how to do live broadcasting in a way that is “content-oriented”?
- China News Network
China News Service, February 11 - The Chinese e-commerce industry has emerged a "new variable", how to do "content is king" to promote?
Xia Bin, a reporter from China Finance News
We entered the e-commerce business late, but we realized from the beginning that to stand out in the sea of millions of stores, content is very important.
"Fong Fang, a "post-90" girl from Guangdong, now runs a food store on Twitch e-commerce, making an offline store with more than 30 years of history "blossom" online.
The video, which is a mimic of the soundtrack of a Hong Kong film, accompanied by classic Cantonese songs, opens the @FangFang one-man-show account on Twitch, and the beautiful video is refreshing to the ears.
Recently, Fang Fang, a representative of quality creators, spoke at the "Search for Peers and Quality Content Sharing" event of Douyin's e-commerce. She shared her experience and feelings in daily creation.
She said: "The video was well-crafted and attracted a lot of attention from netizens, many of whom were interested in my homemade ingredients and wanted to help me make delicious food, and the sales channel opened immediately.
Translation requested.
Fang Fang used to make videos of cooking soup to make more people love the taste of "old Guangzhou", and sold 300,000 units of nourishing food in a single live broadcast, saving the old store that was on the verge of bankruptcy.
“No content, no e-commerce”, as short videos and live broadcast e-commerce continue to develop, people’s requirements and standards for e-commerce content are entering a new stage.
In the early days of livestreaming, the only selling point seemed to be the price advantage, with livestreamers often offering low-priced discounts to attract customers.
In recent years, there have been many phenomenal KOLs, such as Liu Liang Hong and Fan Jia Yuan, as well as many non-mainstream KOLs and merchants who have emerged in the vertical field. They have continuously created high-quality content that matches their brand characteristics, and have improved their long-term operating efficiency.
Gao Yaxuan, the head of the operation of the star author of the video e-commerce of Douyin, introduced that in the past year, 6.27 million creators have turned their content into income through Douyin video e-commerce, and their content creation volume has increased by 252%, and the total sales amount has increased by more than 100%.
“Behind these numbers, we can feel a thriving, vibrant author ecosystem.
Gao Yaxuan said.
The Beijing Normal University Platform for Innovation in Communication and Future Media previously released the ECHI Report on the Content Ecological Health Index of the E-commerce Industry, which analyzed the importance of high-quality content from a data perspective, assessing the content ecological status of 27 major e-commerce platforms domestically using an index system.
According to the report on e-commerce industry content ecosystem health index rankings, Douyin E-commerce, Kuaishou, Tmall, Pinduoduo, and JD rank among the top five.
The report concludes that the content ecosystem of the e-commerce industry is a comprehensive concept that integrates e-commerce with content, but not all content can be integrated with e-commerce, and that good PGC (professional produced content) and UGC (user-generated content) are the quality carriers for integration with e-commerce, and that the higher the value of the content platform, the richer the scenarios for consumption and promotion, the greater the possibility of e-commerce implantation, the stronger the commercial value, and the higher the proportion of e-commerce content production and content consumption that is distributed in this gradually integrated public and private domain.
On-site, Professor Yu Guoming of Beijing Normal University’s School of Journalism and Communication, who is also chairman of the China Media Economics and Management Professional Committee, provided an analysis and interpretation of the report.
He said that in terms of content value, the current e-commerce industry has transitioned from “accessibility to consumption” to “quality-oriented consumption,” and high-quality, professional, and differentiated content is the “hard currency” of the e-commerce industry.
At the same time, content becomes the fundamental and the handle for the new stage of e-commerce development. PGC (Professional Generated Content) content such as knowledge payment, professional knowledge, KOL (Key Opinion Leader) and so on becomes the standard in e-commerce live broadcast.
Looking ahead to the future development of the e-commerce industry, Yu Guomin put forward two suggestions.
One is to promote the overall improvement of the level and quality of e-commerce content eco-health from the perspective of content structure improvement, to create positive content creation and management standards, and to achieve e-commerce content eco-health system index and dynamic balance.
Another one is from the external ecological perspective, to achieve the healthy development of the content e-commerce industry and the value co-creation and co-prosperity with the external environment.
In the future, the e-commerce industry needs more data and artificial intelligence support to predict the stability of the future development; in addition, it needs to provide more standardized and healthy growth space for merchants to realize the value cooperation of enterprises, users, products and services, and create a healthy content ecology.
